\description{
Executes the model training, internal validation, and prediction steps required
to fuse donor survey variables onto American Community Survey (ACS) recipient microdata.
Expects preprocessed input files generated by \code{\link{fusionInput}} to exist on-disk.

\code{fusionOutput_multiyear()} is a convenience wrapper around \code{fusionOutput()} to iteratively run data fusion
models across sequential ACS recipient years. The function automatically passes the
\code{.fsn} model file generated by the prior year's run to accelerate variable selection
and model training for subsequent years.
}
\details{
\code{fusionOutput()} ties together the machine-learning pipeline provided by the \code{fusionModel} package.
Given a valid setup created by \code{\link{fusionInput}}, \code{fusionOutput()} manages the complete modeling lifecycle:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Data Assembly}: Loads harmonized donor predictors, donor target variables (\code{fusion_vars}), and spatial predictor variables matching the donor's survey vintage and geographic boundaries (PUMA 2010 vs. PUMA 2020).
\item \strong{Predictor Selection (\code{prepXY})}: Evaluates feature correlations and screening thresholds via \code{\link[fusionModel]{prepXY}} (or reuses structure from an existing \code{.fsn} file if \code{fsn} is specified).
\item \strong{Model Training (\code{train})}: Trains gradient boosted decision trees via LightGBM using sensible default hyperparameters tuned for production or rapid test runs.
\item \strong{Validation Fusing (\code{fuse})}: If \code{validation = TRUE}, fuses the target variables back onto the training data to create a validation dataset (\code{.fsd}) for downstream evaluation.
\item \strong{Recipient Prediction (\code{fuse})}: Loads ACS microdata, merges spatial context predictors, and fuses \code{M} implicates of the target variables onto the recipient microdata.
